WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.902
Mass evacuations are underway from Sudan

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.004
as the latest cease

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.039
fire agreement is set to expire in

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.207
just hours.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.209
But some people who are desperate

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.010
to flee remain

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.878
of course, trapped, both foreigners

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.246
as well as Sudanese

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.547
with fighting like this

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.782
in Khartoum's densely

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.183
populated neighborhoods.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.652
It is just too dangerous to stay

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.888
but it's also dangerous to leave.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.289
And even once people manage

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.090
to reach safe,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.225
safer ground,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.593
their traumatic ordeals

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.461
are not necessarily over.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.629
Our next guests

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.598
say his parents escape the horrific

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.466
fighting only to find themselves

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.402
in a desperate situation.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.669
The Egyptian border.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.605
Emara is a US citizen.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:39.272
He and his wife

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:42.142
Leila are joining us from San Francisco.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:42.942
Imad and Leila,

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:43.943
thank you very much to you

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.245
both for taking the time

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.247
to speak to us this evening in March.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.782
Just just bring us up to date.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.351
Where is your father right now?

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:53.787
Right now

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.623
they are currently in the RG,

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.959
a border on the Egyptian side

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.294
They are currently stuck.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.563
They can't get into the country.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.864
The Egyptians are denying

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.533
my father access

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.734
to enter Egypt

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.470
so he can come back to America.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.406
And why are they denying him entry?

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.040
Because your mother,

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:14.741
from what I understand,

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.609
your mother can get can go through.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.444
Right.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.979
Yes, my mother can go through.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:20.980
She's an American citizen.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.048
She has a valid U.S.

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.683
passport in Iraq

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.418
while they were fleeing Khartoum,

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.986
you know, fleeing the bombing

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.188
and heavy shelling

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.522
My father lost

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:32.025
his valid American passport

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.992
and he didn't know it

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:33.927
until he got to

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.762
the Sudanese Egyptian passport.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.763
But what he did have

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.897
was his expired

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.199
American passport

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:41.534
and a photocopy of his valid passport.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.970
And that was not enough to allow him

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.371
entry into Egypt.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.240
And they've been stuck at the border

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.708
for the past two days.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.176
The conditions at the border

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.811
are extremely dire.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.113
It's very hot.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:55.882
They didn't have water, no food.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.784
It's a humanitarian crisis.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.185
That's breaking out in the corner.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.020
And we are extremely worried

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.755
about my parents like they did.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.089
You know,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.491
we don't want them to escape

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:05.125
the atrocities

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.326
that are happening in Khartoum

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.027
just to die in the border,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.229
trying to enter and flee

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.263
and come back home to us.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.233
And he's 74.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.602
And with the heat and the conditions

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.837
and the lack of water as you were saying,

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.672
that is incredibly worrying.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.442
So just talk us through the efforts

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.377
that you've been trying to get through

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.312
to trying to get them out.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.547
Who have you spoken to?

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.416
Who have you contacted?

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.485
We've contacted everyone that we know

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.255
that is able to influence the decision.

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.891
We've contacted the consulate in Egypt

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.526
on numerous occasions.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.561
We've contacted the State Department

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.428
multiple times.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.563
We've contacted

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.697
our local congressman

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.133
here in San Francisco as well.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.602
We are doing everything in our power

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.371
to see if we can make a change

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.138
and see if we can.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.040
They can allow my father to enter.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.376
We just need him to enter the country.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.077
So he can come to America.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.746
It doesn't make sense to turn him away.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.248
Now, if they've come so far,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.651
just to be told that they cannot enter

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.085
is frankly unacceptable.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:06.753
And it's appalling.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.856
Your contacts, the

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.857
State Department,

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:11.791
what are they telling you?

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.092
What is the US side

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.094
saying in terms of what they can do

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.532
The US says they're trying their best.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:20.700
They're trying

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.636
to communicate with the embassy, but

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.705
we're not getting a status update

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.074
There's no transparency into the process.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.175
We've asked them all

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.343
times, like, you know what,

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.844
how long this is going to take.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.613
What are the steps that you're taking?

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.081
Even if you were to get approval.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.549
How are you going to contact

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.484
our parents on the ground?

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.352
You know, it's hard to get

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.053
cell phone service

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.654
you can to connect with them.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.190
So everything has been up in the air.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.124
And frankly,

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:45.858
super confusing

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.560
for us as much as our parents

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.796
who are on the ground trying to survive.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.598
And imagine,

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.232
Leila, I mean,

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.100
when was the last time

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.535
you spoke to a father?

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.637
What conversation? What did he tell you?

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.839
What what did he sound like?

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:00.506
Demand.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:05.278
He he sounded extremely anxious,

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.080
deeply worried

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.316
that he might not be able to make it.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.518
He says the conditions there are dire.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.120
There is no food.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.322
He cannot take his medicine without food.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:19.692
You know, he has a health condition,

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.327
a heart condition,

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.596
diabetes, high blood pressure.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.365
Him and my mother are struggling

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:25.898
right now.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.066
They're just in shock

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:27.867
that they're not able

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.469
to enter the country.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.004
And they sound very desperate.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.206
They are very desperate right now.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.607
And your mother can cross this

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.242
of course, I'm guessing here.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:36.843
He doesn't want

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.977
she doesn't want to leave him.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.214
It's hard to leave a loved one.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:41.514
You know,

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.316
it is hard to leave a 74 year

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.484
old man by himself.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.352
In these conditions.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.420
So you're in a situation

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.921
where really, both yourself

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:49.622
and your wife, Leyla,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.590
you kind of hitting your head

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.291
against the wall.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.292
So what is your message

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.294
here to the State Department?

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.330
Our message to department is to

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.366
please help our fellow citizens

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.068
out, allow these Americans

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.503
to enter the country

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.872
so they can seek aid, they can seek help

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:07.607
so they can leave Egypt.

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.143
Our objective is not to stay in Egypt.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.411
We want to bring them back home.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.812
These are American citizens.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.080
We should do everything in our power

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.148
to ensure that they're able

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:16.382
to come back home

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:17.150
and help us

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.718
and also to explore

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.153
ways to cut the bureaucracy.

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:21.821
We're just trying

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.890
to understand how hard it is to contact

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.224
the border,

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.559
to just communicate

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:28.027
that he has a valid passport.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:31.831
So bureaucracy, we can't kill our family.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.866
And we're asking for assistance

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.401
for those on the ground,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.437
for water, food, basic necessities.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:38.071
We understand

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.205
UNHCR and others

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.139
might be working

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.708
to visit the border,

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:43.876
but we're hoping they can act sooner.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.345
And provide desperate supplies

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.846
as soon as possible.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:49.048
It's an incredibly worry for his health

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.083
and for good reasons.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:52.585
It is very hot right now.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.388
This there's an exodus of people leaving,

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.157
aid organizations really struggling,

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.392
a lack of water.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:00.493
We've seen ourselves

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.061
here, intermittent connectivity,

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.496
trying to get

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.397
to speak to people on

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:07.333
the ground is incredibly hard.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.335
And I know your parents went there

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:10.937
for a short amount of time,

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:12.438
right, to Sudan, never

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.340
seeing this coming. I want

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.243
They didn't see it coming.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:17.910
As a matter of fact,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.045
no one saw this coming,

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:21.047
which is extremely surprising

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.615
that no one was warned

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.683
that there was going to be a war

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:25.651
to break out and evacuate the country.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.319
As soon as possible.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:27.320
Typically, there's

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.855
at least a 24 hour notice

00:06:28.855 --> 00:06:31.023
for people to figure out a way to escape.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.961
And and they've gone through a lot

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.363
these past two weeks,

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.365
and they've made it this far.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.134
We're hoping that they can just survive

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:43.102
and this ordeal can come to an end.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.237
This nightmare can come to an end

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.605
for all of us.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.407
Well, we're hoping that, too.

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.876
Please keep us posted in mind.

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:50.676
And Layla,

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:53.246
I hope, of course, that this interview

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.782
helps facilitate

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:57.183
at least the bureaucracy.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:59.585
Get some your father some

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.753
help on the ground.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.088
Please keep us posted.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.656
Imad and Leila, keep us posted on

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:04.624
how he's doing

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:06.659
it'll will be wonderful to speak to him

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.261
when he's on the other side.

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:10.863
And he's caught his breath

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:11.697
and he's relaxed.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:12.799
Thank you very much.

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:14.167
Keeping my fingers crossed for you.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:15.234
Both appreciated.

